| `build_sonice_suivi_de_colis_module.sh` | `PrestaShop-SoNice-Suivi` | `sonice_suivicolis` | `common/` |

`seller_partner/` rules: `module-ignore-seller-partner.mdc`.

## Where `common/*.class.php` comes from

When `BUILD_INTEGRATE_COMMON_DEPS=1` (the default; Amazon legacy on; **Amazon SaaS off**), `build_module.sh` copies:

`C:\Users\Windows 10\projects\prestashop\Prestashop-Marketplaces-Common-Classes`

into the package `common/` folder. Shipped classes:

`tools.class.php` (`CommonTools`), `configuration.class.php`, `configuration_check.class.php`, `certificates.class.php`, `cart.class.php`, `order.class.php`, `support.class.php`, `validate.class.php`, `zip.class.php`.

Marketplace classes such as `classes/cdiscount.tools.class.php` **require** those files. They do not define them.

```php
// ❌ BAD — file is not in the module repo; the next build replaces common/
// editing PrestaShop-Cdiscount/common/tools.class.php

// ✅ GOOD — shared helper for every marketplace that injects common/
// editing Prestashop-Marketplaces-Common-Classes/tools.class.php
// then: ./build_cdiscount_module.sh
```

## Where to change a class

| You need to change | Edit |
|---|---|
| `CommonTools` or another `common/*.class.php` for every module that injects `common/` | `Prestashop-Marketplaces-Common-Classes`, then rebuild each affected module |
| Behaviour of one marketplace only | That module's own `classes/`, `functions/`, `controllers/` — not a copy of the shared class |
| Amazon SaaS `common/` | `Prestashop-SAAS-Module/common/` (committed; build does not refresh it from Common-Classes) |
| `classes/seller_partner/` | `shopify-amazon-spapi-connector`, then copy the changed files into every source-tree `seller_partner/` that exists, then `build_amazon_module.sh` or `build_amazon_saas_module.sh` |

If the module git tree already contains `common/<file>`, that copy is rsync'd **on top** of Common-Classes and wins for that module only. Use an overlay only for a deliberate one-module fork. Amazon gitignores `/common/` — do not commit fixes there.

## Sync seller_partner copies

Connector path: `C:\Users\Windows 10\projects\shopify\shopify-amazon-spapi-connector`

After changing a file there, copy that same relative path to:

- `C:\Users\Windows 10\projects\prestashop\Prestashop-SAAS-Module\classes\seller_partner\`
- `C:\Users\Windows 10\projects\prestashop\Prestashop-Amazon\classes\seller_partner\` when that directory exists (legacy Amazon gitignores it; skip if absent)

Copy file contents. Keep copy-only lines that are already part of that tree, such as `if (!defined('_PS_VERSION_')) { exit; }` on PHP files that have it. Do not invent module-only behavior in the copy.

The ZIP still comes from the connector at build time. The copy is so source checkouts match the connector before the next build.

## Do not

- Patch a generated package directory or ZIP. The build deletes the package dir after zipping.
- Add `common/tools.class.php` (or the other shared classes) into a module repo to "fix" a missing file. Point the change at Common-Classes.
- Assume Amazon SaaS picks up a Common-Classes edit. Its build leaves `common/` as stored in `Prestashop-SAAS-Module`.
